<title>GERMANY: Rosenthal plans to scrap voting right limit.</title>
<headline>Rosenthal plans to scrap voting right limit.</headline>
<dateline>SELB, Germany 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German porcelain manufacturer Rosenthal AG said it planned to propose to shareholders that a regulation capping the voting rights of shareholders should be scrapped.</p>
<p>The company currently allows individual shareholders to command a vote of no more than five percent, regardless of the number of shares actually held.</p>
<p>The announcement was made in conjunction with news that Rosenthal plans to raise its capital by 10 percent to allow Ireland's Waterford Wedgwood to take a stake in the German firm.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
